analysisWe need to produce assert statement for comment after removeFirstOccurrence method.

Comment: "// @@@ If the deque originally contained the specified element, then the result is true."

Interpretation: If before the method call, the deque contained o, then the method returns true. So specification: (\old(this.contains(o))) => \result == true. Also maybe need to consider null? The method returns false if o null or not contained. But comment only says if originally contained, then result is true. So assert: \old(this.contains(o)) => \result == true. Could also write => \result. In JML, boolean true can be omitted? Usually assert \old(this.contains(o)) => \result; but to be explicit: \old(this.contains(o)) => \result == true. Use \result variable.

Thus final code:

<code>assert \old(this.contains(o)) => \result == true;</code>

Check syntax: Need parentheses? Not necessary. Provide as code block.

